.TH BACKGROUND 2 2000-1月 "cluster_names" "cluster_names"
.SH NAME
cluster_names \- Get the cluster name of each gene id from the given background model.
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fIcluster_names(\fBbackground\fR as <generic> Background, 
\fBidset\fR as any);\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Get the cluster name of each gene id from the given background model.
.PP
.SH OPTIONS
.PP
\fBbackground\fB \fR\- the GSEA background model object.. 
.PP
.PP
\fBidset\fB \fR\- 
 a character vector of the gene ids, the first cluster that contains the target
 gene will be used for query the cluster name.
. 
.PP
.SH VALUE
.PP
a character vector of the cluster name of each input gene id, a \fBNULL\fR value will be
 returned for the gene id that is not annotated in any cluster.
.PP
.SH DETAILS
.PP
This function returns only the first matched cluster name when a gene is annotated
 in multiple clusters, use \fBgeneSet.intersects\fR with \fBget_clusterID=TRUE\fR for
 getting all of the cluster ids of the gene.
.PP
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
let kb = read.background("hsa.xml");
 print(cluster_names(kb, c("7157", "1956")));
.PP
.SH SEE ALSO
background
.SH FILES
.PP
gseakit.dll
.PP
